metacircular-univalent-unison-of-cubically-receptive-stateboxes-lines-9 = cons "In hyperactivity the hash is the reference. Code lives in the store: one reader hashes what is on disk at bootstrap, and from then on the hash is the reference. The store holds every value under its hash; the names log records who pointed which name at which content, and when. That log is version control, finer than a tree of files. One realtime server over one store serves the command line, the public works and wiki, and the hosting of source; each is a view of the same values, and publishing is pointing a public name at a value." (cons "" nil)
